messages:
nora: FYI I observed duplicate webhook calls from sampleapp when the SDK hit a 429 during a token rotation. Two POSTs with identical bodies ~1.2s apart.

li: Oof. Which SDK and sampleapp config? streaming or non-streaming?

nora: Node SDK (v0.11.4) with streaming flow enabled in sampleapp-local. Non-streaming webhook handler on our side, so we saw two identical deliveries.

nora: Repro I used: start local sampleapp, set token TTL very short, run a tight loop of /generate requests. Force a token refresh in the middle.

nora: Minimal client wrapper that triggers it:
```js
// client retry snippet
async function send(payload){
  try{
    const res = await fetch(apiUrl, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(payload), headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } });
    if(res.status === 429) throw new Error('RATE');
    return res.json();
  }catch(e){
    // current behavior: immediate retry without idempotency header
    await sleep(200);
    return send(payload);
  }
}
```

nora: Notice there's no Idempotency-Key header and the retry is immediate (fixed sleep). That makes duplicates likely if the server accepted the first request but client retried.

tom: Can you paste the two request-ids from the receiver logs?

nora: receiver logs: 2026-03-21T09:03:10Z req=rx_9c1a received body len=650 
2026-03-21T09:03:11.221Z req=rx_9c1b received body len=650

sasha: 1.2s gap. Matches a quick retry after token refresh. My guess: when we rotate tokens we briefly break connection so the SDK retries. If server already processed the first POST, duplicate happens.

li: Short-term mitigations: add randomized exponential backoff (jitter) + attach Idempotency-Key on POSTs. Also change sampleapp to wait for a final delivery ack from our webhook dispatcher before returning success in streaming mode (avoid early ack).

sasha: Agree. Also add a client-side replay window: when retrying, include the original request id in a header (X-Original-Request) and the server can dedupe for a short TTL.

ops-bot: incident-alert: duplicate-delivery-rate > 0.5% for sampleapp-demo - triggered at 09:10:00Z

li: I'll draft a small patch to the Node SDK that: 1) enables jittered exponential backoff by default for 429, 2) adds optional Idempotency-Key generation for POSTs, and 3) exposes a safeReplay opt-in flag that waits for final ack.

nora: Please include a clear opt-out and make it opt-in for now (we don't want to change behavior for all users). Also add telemetry to measure how often the safeReplay path is taken.

dev-bot: ci: queued tests for redwood/sampleapp#456 (branch: safe-replay)

li: I'll also add an e2e test in the harness that simulates token expiry mid-request and asserts a single webhook call. This should catch regressions in SDKs.

tom: Can we ensure parity? Go and Python SDKs should implement the same header and backoff defaults. Let's add a checklist item to the devex SDK parity doc.

sasha: I'll file a short RFC in the devex repo outlining the replay guard, idempotency header semantics, and suggested TTLs for server-side dedupe.

nora: For immediate ops: I've enabled idempotency header in our internal webhook forwarder and relaxed the demo cluster token TTL to reduce rotations. Monitoring in place for duplicates > 0 within 10s.

li: Thanks. Follow-ups: I'll send PR for Node SDK (w/ tests), add e2e harness test, tom to update parity checklist, sasha to write RFC. Ping me if you see duplicates after the canary. :raised_hands:
